From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 73/73] PC5: read-only files past a budget parked and opened again
 when needed, as a title opens only about 250 files however high its limit
 (Leo Lobato's Wine patch 0993)

Games that keep hundreds of archives open (Unreal's packages, an older game's .upk files) failed with "Too many open files": raising RLIMIT_NOFILE (patch 0071) doesn't raise how many files a PS5 title can open. Leo Lobato's prospero-win patch 0993 parks the least recently used read-only files past a budget and opens them again by name, as patch 0871 does for directories.
